# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Cerise post-mortem gate: kernel crashlog survives a warm reboot.
#
# Boots //products:x64-crashlog (x64-smoke + a ZBI_TYPE_NVRAM ram-crashlog region
# + kernel.cerise-test-crashlog=true) via the direct-kernel path in ONE QEMU
# session run WITHOUT -no-reboot, so a guest panic warm-reboots the same kernel
# image (QEMU DRAM survives system_reset). The self-terminating recovery-gated
# hook (zircon/kernel/platform/pc/platform.cc) panics on the cold boot and, on the
# warm reboot, recovers+prints the stowed crashlog. The test asserts, IN ORDER,
# the live panic then the recovered crashlog with SW reason KERNEL PANIC and the
# intentional-panic message (proving the crashlog CONTENT survived), and that
# exactly one panic fired (no panic/reboot loop).
sh_test(
    name = "crashlog-boot",
    srcs = ["crashlog_boot.sh"],
    args = [
        "$(rootpath @qemu_x86_64//:qemu-system-x86_64)",
